5981	    /// The representations the apprt could serve for the request's MIME
5982	    /// types. These are immediately copied as needed so they only need
5983	    /// to live for the duration of the completion call. Requesters that
5984	    /// only carry text (paste, OSC 52) use the first text-like
5985	    /// representation.
5986	    contents: []const terminal.clipboard.Content = &.{},
5987	
5988	    /// The listing of MIME types available on the clipboard, only
5989	    /// gathered when the request asked for it.
5990	    available: []const []const u8 = &.{},
5991	
5992	    /// True if any clipboard confirmation prompt was already answered
5993	    /// by the user, skipping further prompts:
5994	    ///
5995	    ///   - For "regular" pasting this means that unsafe pastes are
5996	    ///     allowed. Unsafe data is defined as data that contains
5997	    ///     line terminators (newlines or carriage returns), though
5998	    ///     this definition may change later to detect other scenarios.
5999	    ///
6000	    ///   - For OSC 52 and Kitty clipboard protocol reads and writes no
6001	    ///     prompt is shown to the user when this is true.
6002	    confirmed: bool = false,
6003	
6004	    /// True if the user asked to remember their decision. This is only
6005	    /// honored by request types that support session grants (Kitty
6006	    /// clipboard protocol requests carrying a password).
6007	    remember: bool = false,
